WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.320
Communications and user activity artifacts are often important in iPhone investigations.

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:21.220
iMessage and SMS records, call history, contacts, voicemail metadata at a high level, mail artifacts, Safari records, app usage indicators, notifications, keyboard artifacts, and autofill-related traces can all help build context.

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:24.160
The risk is overclaiming what those artifacts prove.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:34.940
iMessage and SMS concepts include message content where available, participants, timestamps, attachments, service type, status, and account context.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:46.440
A message record may show that a communication existed, but additional evidence may be needed to determine whether it was read, acted on, deleted, synchronized, or produced by a particular device.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:51.780
Attachments and reactions can add useful detail but still require timeline correlation.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:57.040
Call history, contacts, and voicemail records can help identify relationships and events.

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:03.740
A call log may show attempted, missed, incoming, or outgoing communication depending on available fields.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:09.480
Contacts may be created directly, imported, synchronized, or added by an application.

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:15.060
Voicemail artifacts may show metadata or content depending on acquisition scope and service behavior.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:24.400
Safari and app usage artifacts can include browsing history, tabs, downloads, cookies, search records, cached data, or usage indicators.

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:30.940
These may reflect direct activity, background loading, redirects, shared account synchronization, or application state.

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:37.000
Notifications can show that information reached the device, but not always whether the user saw or acted on it.

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:42.020
A disciplined analyst differentiates local device evidence from cloud-synced account activity.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:48.480
They avoid unsupported claims about who performed a specific action unless the evidence supports that level of attribution.

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:57.900
Communications and activity artifacts are strongest when correlated with lock state, account logs, app records, device timelines, and independent evidence.
